### Object of the invention

The invention provides a single, closed-processing apparatus capable of emulsifying, dispersing, dissolving, atomizing, mixing, or stirring liquids and fluid–solid mixtures. It is intended to produce rapid, uniform treatment while operating selectively under pressure, at atmospheric pressure, or under vacuum, thereby limiting aeration, contamination, solvent loss, and unwanted foaming.

### Configuration

The apparatus comprises:

- a pressure- and vacuum-resistant processing vessel with a removable or sealed cover;
- one or more fluid and powder inlets, a product outlet, and pressure, vacuum, venting, and cleaning connections;
- a motor-driven shaft extending into the vessel through a pressure-tight rotary seal;
- a replaceable working head mounted on the shaft, such as a rotor–stator homogenizer, impeller, turbine, propeller, dispersing disk, or atomizing element;
- stationary baffles or a stator surrounding the rotating member to generate shear, turbulence, circulation, and particle-size reduction;
- an optional recirculation conduit that withdraws material from the vessel and returns it through the working head or an atomizing nozzle;
- a heating or cooling jacket for controlling product temperature; and
- controls for rotational speed, vessel pressure, vacuum level, temperature, flow rate, and processing time.

During operation, rotation of the working head draws fluid and added ingredients into a high-shear region, where they are divided, accelerated, and repeatedly recirculated. Different attachments and operating speeds allow the same unit to perform low-speed stirring, high-shear dispersion and emulsification, dissolution of powders, or atomization into droplets. The sealed vessel permits the selected operation to be carried out under pressurized, atmospheric, or evacuated conditions.
